    "body": "The effect is precisely defined by the data model here, so I would avoid the use of \"possible\" or \"likely\" here.  What about this...\r\n`This means the <span>sticky activation</span> state spans multiple navigations as long as the same <span>Document</span> gets reused.  For the transient activation state, the original <span>expiry</span> time remains unchanged (i.e. the state still expires within the <span>transient activation duration</span> limit from the _original_ <span>activation triggering input event</span>).`",
